nd gestures or speaking dead tongues while he's doing his hand flames. Setting aside that this has never been an issue (regardless of what Brucato apparently thinks) - the &amp;quot;wizard&amp;quot; could always be a crazy person who <i>coincidentally</i> had things go his way - greater tech and the geek culture age have given us a ready excuse for this. Obviously, the person shooting fire from his hand (who &amp;quot;of course&amp;quot; has a hidden wrist-mounted flamethrower) is a nerd who is <i>role-playing</i> a wizard. Because that's just the kind of shit us nerds get up to these days.<br /> <br /> Which, yes, makes this a case of a wizard pretending to be a normal bloke <i>pretending to be a wizard</i>. Coincidental Magick by way of meta recursion.<br /> <br /> This is just one example. A mystic doesn't need to dabble into technomancy herself to reap the benefits of the high tech age. They totally CAN do that, and there are plenty of advantages to doing so. But for a &amp;quot;vanilla&amp;quot; mystic, a wrist-mounted flamethrower is little different from the lighters and cans of hair spray they relied on in the 90s. Except folks have become so jaded about technology, a mystic barely need affect the impression of having it.<br /> <br /> <br /> On a more serious note, the Technocracy is in trouble because of the steady erosion of the concept of Objective Truth. Photographs, videos, audio, arguably even human senses can be fabricated, altered, or fooled. People argue over basic facts - whether it's the actions of politicians or the roundness of the Earth - in a manner unheard of before. It often feels as though, despite the increasing interconnectedness of society, people seem to live in more and more disparate realities. The very idea of there being a &amp;quot;Truth&amp;quot; that can be known is under siege.<br /> <br /> This is not a good thing for the Technocracy. Their goals have, from the word go, revolved around creating a single, universal Consensus of what Reality is and what it is not. For the Order of Reason, it was their One World, One Church. For the modern Union, it's not different. They want a unified belief. More than ever, though, it seems like technology is making it <i>harder</i> to standardize people's impressions of Reality, rather than easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to post something, but <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> expressed most of what I thought better than I would have. Nice. I'd add, though, that the Blatancy Ability would cover so, so much more than ever for mages that slip technology into their Magick in some way. Coincidental fireballs? Sure thing... <i>For starters.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T08:39:32-07:00","id":1227673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1227663#post1227663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Putting it this way, it's like the high tech age is slowly becoming the new mythic age.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine how crazy things could get if that happens. I mean, KRISPR/CAS-9 giving people the ability to change their genes by getting what amount to a shot is able to make most life effects coincidental or even mundane. Fusion power could, in a round about way, do the same with forces effects by making electricity so available and cheap that we can use it for everyone's crazy ideas.<br /> <br /> I guess the virtual adepts were partially right, we're entering mythic age 2.0. Where Everyone and their dog has the power, not just the king's high wizard(though in modern day he'll still have More power unfortunately, money tends to do that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T12:58:25-07:00","id":1227730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1227673#post1227673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine how crazy things could get if that happens. I mean, KRISPR/CAS-9 giving people the ability to change their genes by getting what amount to a shot is able to make most life effects coincidental or even mundane.</div> </div> </div> </div>It always depends on what the mage has to do to get the effect. Stuff like that is absolute GOLD for a Mage who does not need a tool anymore for the effect - just take a syringe with something harmless, stick it in, silently cast a Life effect.<br /> But someone like a young Verbena who has to do some chants and dances to heal somebody is going to have a hard time hiding the fact.<br /> <br /> But, yes, Mages who do not depend too much on ritualistic Magic are able to hide as much behind mundane technology as the Technocrats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 06-15-2018, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T13:25:46-07:00","id":1227736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1227663#post1227663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Putting it this way, it's like the high tech age is slowly becoming the new mythic age.</div> </div> </div> </div>When sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic, it becomes impossible to prove that magic wasn't just tech, or vice versa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T13:33:58-07:00","id":1227739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1227736#post1227736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic, it becomes impossible to prove that magic wasn't just tech, or vice versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that must constantly annoy the Technocracy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T14:15:49-07:00","id":1227749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1227663#post1227663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Putting it this way, it's like the high tech age is slowly becoming the new mythic age.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point! I hadn't thought of any of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T14:29:53-07:00","id":1227753,"title":"","content":"We shouldn't just focus on tech here; the economy and social experience have transformed.<br /> <br /> Cryptocurrency, a renaissance of ponzi/pyramid schemes, outrage culture online*... people will believe a LOT thanks to how the internet distorts perception of the world.<br /> <br /> Getting rich in a few days through shady dark web investments? Is that really vulgar? Getting millions to attack an abuser, or abused person? Definitely coincidental. Tricking thousands of people into your scam? Entirely believable.<br /> <br /> <i>* I should point out that when I say &quot;outrage culture&quot;, I'm being even-handed. Everything from &quot;wow I can't believe this person said this mildly problematic thing in ignorance, let's put this person on trial&quot; to &quot;wow I'm deeply offended that they put a woman in a thing, better rouse the townsfolk and grab our pitchforks&quot;. It's not even a matter of people being furious over things they shouldn't be furious over. Being outraged doesn't make you right or wrong, after all; sometimes being outraged is the right response! But I think most observers can agree that creating a huge mob online and deconstructing a person's life, for good or ill, is coincidental thanks to the internet.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 06-15-2018, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T15:04:11-07:00","id":1227764,"title":"","content":"Modern Magick, Modern Paradox:<br /> <br /> James wants to ruin his ex's life. So he hacks into their facebook or twitter using mundane abilities, and creates a post. The content of the post should be inflammatory in one way or another; a simplified strawman of a progressive or conservative political stance, a racist or homophobic joke, a hot take on a really complex and controversial event...<br /> <br /> He then uses Mind 2 and Entropy 2, along with Correspondence/Data 2, to implant several subtle effects onto this digital foundation. With Mind 2 he implants an impulse to spread the content, along with an impulse which heightens awareness and dampens inhibition. When people see this, this is going to be the worst or best thing they've ever seen. So if it's a racist joke it's going to be shared on every racist and reprehensible platform, and universally reviled otherwise. With Entropy 2 he nudges the strands of the digital web in his favour, helps the post find the path of least resistance. With Entropy 1 and Data 1 he might seek out the absolute best way to make the post, the language and timing, the hashtags, figuring out what will give the best possible result.<br /> <br /> James succeeds in this ritual, and the post goes viral. His ex's life is ruined. The scholarship they had won is withdrawn, they lose their job, friends desert them, and a simple google search will make most employers throw her CV into the bin. This is almost impossible to undo if James were to regret it however.<br /> <br /> But say James were to botch the ritual? The backlash could be quite interesting. A paradox spirit might manifest within the digital web, and kidnap James into it. Judgement Gone Viral. This manifestation of Judgement is concerned with his own online behaviour. His embarrassing porn habits, the edgy jokes he made on deleted chatboards when he was 14, the fanfiction and slashfiction he wrote... all of it is laid bare for the world to see. All of his attempts to undo this, hide it, just make it worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T15:20:20-07:00","id":1227769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1227655#post1227655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes change in consensus, no I don't know how to cover it. I don't know how to make it so your IXers cyberware is now something that a mundane surgeon can work on. I don't know how to make it so hedge magic just becomes &quot;Mundane&quot; skills like the various sciences over time. I don't know how to represent superstitions and urban legends becoming more true as belief spreads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... perhaps expand on the Reality Zones system, by creating levels. A reality zone has a tolerance for technology and a tolerance for mysticism, represented as two ratings from 0 to 10. 0 in Mystic represents a Revised Mage take; the people here are consumed by mass media and technocratic control. They don't believe in mysticism at all, and so the tolerance for coincidental mystic magick is very low. Sensory effects, and &quot;hidden&quot; effects, such as pulling money out of your pocket thanks to a mystical teleportation spell, are fine, but anything overt will not fly unless you set up a convincing cover. 10 in Mystic represents total acceptance of the weird and the wonderful; the people here have absolutely no pretense of understanding how the world works as a whole, and believe that spirits can upheave reality at any time.<br /> <br /> That rating from 0 to 10 effects the burden of Permadox a Mage might carry, whilst also advising the ST on vulgarity and coincidence, and the extent to which paradox strikes back at a Mage.<br /> <br /> For example, within a Technocracy Lab or Construct (Techno = 10, Mystic = 0) cyborgs with enhancements will have their Permadox reduced to 0 regardless of how extensive their enhancements are. And within a mystical Sanctum (Mystic = 10, Techno = 0) a Mage blighted with Permadox due to their curled goats horns and their fiery burning eyes might experience 0 Permadox.<br /> <br /> Outside of these spaces, and a Universal Ascension, reality zones are in the 1-9 range. The exact mechanics of this... well I have plenty of ideas, but I see huge problems with all of them.<br /> <br /> In essence, the ascension war is a competition to push these ratings up or down across the world. If everywhere accepted technomagick up to a rating of 9, then cyborgs riding jetpacks while firing plasma bolts would be okay. That isn't normal tech, but people in these settings would have fully accepted that &quot;special government prototypes&quot; are capable of such activity, and not yet available to the public.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 06-15-2018, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T20:19:35-07:00","id":1227806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1227483#post1227483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're taking the wrong angle:<br /> <br /> WoD simulates reality up to a point, but it's far from accurate. Just see the debates around falling damage and admire how WoD representation of phisics allows normal humans to survive falls from planes and skycrappers without needing to fall on something soft. You don't need to be too realist.<br /> <br /> Computers were always much better at solving certain problems than humans, you shouldn't use the same scale and systems. A NORMAL computer isn't going to roll and risk failing or succeeding each time you want to calculate the square root of phi, that's not realistic - unles very bizarre circumnstances happen (like a blackout) a computer it's going to calculate the value up to the point it was programmed to be able to do so. The difference with a Quantum Computer isn't going to be the &quot;success chance&quot; but rather the &quot;amount&quot;: it should give the answer with a greater degree of accuracy, or faster.<br /> <br /> The easiest way to adjust the system it's the same that you use right now to check, in game, the chance of success of a calculator when a player imputs a calculation - you don't roll for the calculator - if anything, you roll for the character (to see if she understands the problem) with a bonus because she's using a calculator. Extrapolating to Quantum, just determine how much time a normal PC would take to solve the problem with the right imput, and then divide by 300. If rolls are necessary at all, just give the character a bonus (it doesn't need to be proportional with the difference between Digital and Quantum, because the factor of failure it's more the user imput than anything else).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the &quot;using the calculator&quot; argument breaks down a bit when you start getting into things like AI, who will be using the memory and processing power of said computer as their wits/intelligence score. When said AI can implement thousands of versions of itself onto as single task that are simultaneously all the same AI with one goal, the situation becomes the same.<br /> <br /> Considering that the process of creating AI is well documented, heavily used by many companies, and is possible for anyone with the know-how, Mind 5: Create AI is already a mundane effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T21:11:02-07:00","id":1228201,"title":"","content":"Dealing with real world technology has always required a fair bit of suspension of disbelief, because let's be honest: attacks against the powerful rarely succeed, and even more rarely are gotten away with. Technology was at the point where the plucky rebel can't win against people who can afford the best tech a long time ago. Most crimes that are gotten away with are performed against people with no money and no power. If it looks like the rich and powerful are being beaten by the poor and powerless, it usually turns out that someone else rich and powerful is behind it. There could be entire videos done in the style of the What Should Have Happened youtube videos about how some attempt to attack a technocracy place or even just a rich enemy's place should have failed, or succeeded but then almost immediately resulted in the players being jailed, but they succeeded and escaped because who wants to roleplay life imprisonment?<br /> <br /> In other words, games will deal with it the way they always have: by fudging things in the name of a good story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T07:46:33-07:00","id":1228584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1227806#post1227806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the &quot;using the calculator&quot; argument breaks down a bit when you start getting into things like AI, who will be using the memory and processing power of said computer as their wits/intelligence score. When said AI can implement thousands of versions of itself onto as single task that are simultaneously all the same AI with one goal, the situation becomes the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant it's that some stuff may be better represented without the 1 to 5 Attribute rolls because these are intended to represent a human (even animals are often misrepresented by this system -&gt; elephants with Strenght 7, cats with Strenght 1 - theoretically 7 cats can pile on an elephant and grapple it, but I'm disgressing).<br /> <br /> Human make mistakes, a lot of mistakes, you can always rationalize failure as that. Now, If a common calculator doesn't make mistakes (unless the user makes them), why should we 'roll' to see the successes of an AI?. Perhaps it's better to just determine what it can do and assign it as a bonus (or a penalty) on a roll (shit in/shit out it's still true to AI) or a pile of automatic succeses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Considering that the process of creating AI is well documented, heavily used by many companies, and is possible for anyone with the know-how, Mind 5: Create AI is already a mundane effect. </div> </div> </div>Well, this it's very true, but that's not what I meant: Compare with atomic bombs. I can see getting Forces 5 to summon Nuclear Power being a useful and powerful investment because you can't go to the grocery store and buy one - waiving the processes needed to make one of these mass destruction jewels it's powerful!<br /> <br /> The know-how to create trully badass, Google level, AI isn't yet common knowledge, you need Google-level resources and specialists - but soon AI may be so common that needing master level to make them would seem...underwhelming (imagine needing Force Mastery to throw a fireball, which you can do with a flamethrower). Heck, it already is underwhelming, and that's why we have a thread about making AI with lower levels of Mind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-19-2018, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T05:11:17-07:00","id":1228830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1228201#post1228201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dealing with real world technology has always required a fair bit of suspension of disbelief, because let's be honest: attacks against the powerful rarely succeed, and even more rarely are gotten away with. Technology was at the point where the plucky rebel can't win against people who can afford the best tech a long time ago. Most crimes that are gotten away with are performed against people with no money and no power. If it looks like the rich and powerful are being beaten by the poor and powerless, it usually turns out that someone else rich and powerful is behind it. There could be entire videos done in the style of the What Should Have Happened youtube videos about how some attempt to attack a technocracy place or even just a rich enemy's place should have failed, or succeeded but then almost immediately resulted in the players being jailed, but they succeeded and escaped because who wants to roleplay life imprisonment?<br /> <br /> In other words, games will deal with it the way they always have: by fudging things in the name of a good story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah sadly we're at the point where the very nature of technology, and the way the police have been militarized, means that even if a revolution were entirely just, and provoked by the most extreme injustice possible, it would likely be crushed.<br /> <br /> &quot;Revolutions&quot; in a contemporary sense, even in countries where the technology isn't that astounding and the infrastructure isn't that developed, are coups being spun as revolutions. The people don't storm the palace without some faction of the military *allowing* them to storm the palace. So very little actually changes.<br /> <br /> In the case of the Technocracy, the only reason PCs can resist them at all is because they are Literal Wizards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T08:12:24-07:00","id":1228859,"title":"","content":"Well, it is strange and flawed way that MtAs presents itself at all. Technocrats =/= technology, magic isn't anti science and paradigm or humans aren't rational and logical. Technocrats aren't scientists, they follow Scientism, socialism and control. Mages aren't anti-science, they were the first scientists to begin with and developed many fundamental technologies.<br /> <br /> To begin with faith, mysticism and occult are actually in ascendance due to ease of information spreading, spiritual longing and greater appeal then dry 'science'. Scientific discoveries are adapted to integrate into mystic teachings and vice-versa, manga, fiction, movies and etc. jade subconscious minds to tolerate mystical (despite what official line is), value of religion is rediscovered, spirits moved from totem poles to logos and trademarks, and much, much more. <br /> <br /> To add to it, humans are intrinsically irrational and mythic creatures, so what form new development will take - nobody knows. Magic will change, of that there is no doubt, but it seems it's coming back rather then going away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T05:34:59-07:00","id":1229131,"title":"","content":"when you think about it, the main point of contrition between 'science' and 'magic' is existence of Spirit. in WoD where spirit is explicitly given difference between science and magic boils down to difference in methodologies. nothing more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T10:16:22-07:00","id":1229174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1228830#post1228830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah sadly we're at the point where the very nature of technology, and the way the police have been militarized, means that even if a revolution were entirely just, and provoked by the most extreme injustice possible, it would likely be crushed.<br /> <br /> &quot;Revolutions&quot; in a contemporary sense, even in countries where the technology isn't that astounding and the infrastructure isn't that developed, are coups being spun as revolutions. The people don't storm the palace without some faction of the military *allowing* them to storm the palace. So very little actually changes.<br /> <br /> In the case of the Technocracy, the only reason PCs can resist them at all is because they are Literal Wizards.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a more optimistic note, one thing the world has going for it is the free access to information and the inherent empathy/separation of the first world from most violence making it harder to kill each other. If something socially big enough that the world's notoriously Laissez Faire first world population decided to revolt, said police would likely by right behind/beside said population. It'd just end with the same coup d'etat that'd happen in many &quot;Revolutions&quot;, as anyone with power(that's also smart enough to keep it) knows that winning the Ire of the populace is a road to headaches and set-backs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T08:18:57-07:00","id":1229371,"title":"","content":"Just finished reading Magic A Very Short Introduction (Owen Davies) and would like to share with you this closing paragraph: <br /> <br /> 'Magic cannot be consigned to the past, dismissed as the product of ignorance, or ranked as an<br /> evolutionary stage of human thought \u2013 at least not in cultural terms. As this Very Short Introduction<br /> demonstrates, since it was first expressed conceptually back in antiquity, it has accrued a range of<br /> meanings that ensure it retains its relevance in every society today. Magic is far more than a venerable<br /> collection of practices. We need to understand it as a language, a theory, a belief, an action, a creative<br /> expression, an experience, and a cognitive tool. It is integral to religion and yet can be independent of<br /> it. An atheist can believe in magic. Yes, science has undermined the basis of magic as an explanation<br /> for natural processes. It has rendered magic\u2019s role in medicine largely redundant by providing<br /> clearly superior results \u2013 for those of us who can profit from them. But while science gives us<br /> explanations and solutions, it also provides us with a choice. It can help explain magic but cannot<br /> explain it away \u2013 magic is always an alternative. In its broadest sense, magic is a part of the human<br /> condition. To believe magic will eventually disappear is mere wishful thinking.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T14:29:34-07:00","id":1229454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions#post1227452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It makes one wonder how the WOD and by extension the technocracy are reacting to/involved in said changes. What are the traditions going to do about technology coming reaching out and evolving in ways that could rival or even surpass the spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is possible to create what is called a quantum computer.<br /> Using this as an example - the technology used and developed by mundane humans won't get close to what Mages are capable of with Magick.<br /> <br /> Also, mundane human technology has one large limitation - it needs a source of power, like electricity for example, to work. And it also needs maintenence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T14:22:27-07:00","id":1229648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1229454#post1229454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it is possible to create what is called a quantum computer.<br /> Using this as an example - the technology used and developed by mundane humans won't get close to what Mages are capable of with Magick.<br /> <br /> Also, mundane human technology has one large limitation - it needs a source of power, like electricity for example, to work. And it also needs maintenence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the Spheres will always have the advantage that they don't *need* to truly, definitely make sense*. Even the most rigid paradigm has some hand-waving, identifying &quot;enlightened&quot; scientists as being capable of things sleepers won't be able to do.<br /> <br /> But there will come a time where sleeper-tech is sufficiently well developed that with some preparation and resources, a sleeper can achieve much of what an adept Mage can do. They might not have all of the flexibility of a Mage, but things will get more tight.<br /> <br /> * &quot;real world&quot; sense, of course most magick makes sense to the Mage casting it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 06-23-2018, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T10:36:14-07:00","id":1230585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1229648#post1229648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there will come a time where sleeper-tech is sufficiently well developed that with some preparation and resources, a sleeper can achieve much of what an adept Mage can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know if this idea is discussed and/or suggested anywhere in the M:tA books ? I don't recall such an idea being mentioned in any M:tA book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T13:05:38-07:00","id":1230624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1230585#post1230585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you know if this idea is discussed and/or suggested anywhere in the M:tA books ? I don't recall such an idea being mentioned in any M:tA book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I swear a lot of the fluff in M20 talks about this, even if only indirectly? But I can't recall any chapters which explore it explicitly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T06:37:16-07:00","id":1230789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1230624#post1230624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I swear a lot of the fluff in M20 talks about this, even if only indirectly? But I can't recall any chapters which explore it explicitly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the fluff of the Technocracy since the Order of Reason was always to allow sleepers to access the benefits of magic trough their devices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T01:47:03-07:00","id":1231050,"title":"","content":"Giving sleepers the wonders of magic via devices seems to me at least to be a different thing than 'surpassing the spheres'. I mean sleepers can already drop nukes or fire explosive tank shells or kill people with drones...doesn't mean that mages focusing on Forces are rendered irrelevant. (Besides, even if direct damage output is surpassed there's a lot of exotic bullshit mage can pull out like probability manipulation, telepathy etc that its going to be a lot harder to surpass).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T07:33:54-07:00","id":1231103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furoan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1231050#post1231050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Giving sleepers the wonders of magic via devices seems to me at least to be a different thing than 'surpassing the spheres'. I mean sleepers can already drop nukes or fire explosive tank shells or kill people with drones...doesn't mean that mages focusing on Forces are rendered irrelevant. (Besides, even if direct damage output is surpassed there's a lot of exotic bullshit mage can pull out like probability manipulation, telepathy etc that its going to be a lot harder to surpass).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, of course, this had to be said.<br /> <br /> And I don't think direct damage it's surpassed either, at 70 or so aggravated to everything in the area (hard, but reachable) nothing can stand, you wouldn't notice the difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T07:37:01-07:00","id":1231104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furoan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1231050#post1231050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Giving sleepers the wonders of magic via devices seems to me at least to be a different thing than 'surpassing the spheres'. I mean sleepers can already drop nukes or fire explosive tank shells or kill people with drones...doesn't mean that mages focusing on Forces are rendered irrelevant. (Besides, even if direct damage output is surpassed there's a lot of exotic bullshit mage can pull out like probability manipulation, telepathy etc that its going to be a lot harder to surpass).</div> </div> </div> </div>But for all we know technology will reach a point where telepathy and prediction of outcomes (and manipulating them) fall within the range of technology.<br /> <br /> Sure it seems absurd now, but a metal egg that can completely destabilize the environment and the politics of the whole world, while killing millions, seems patently ridiculous, as does a little rectangle that lets you speak with anyone in the world who has another one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T10:14:34-07:00","id":1231142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1231104#post1231104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But for all we know technology will reach a point where telepathy and prediction of outcomes (and manipulating them) fall within the range of technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is possible at all in regards to telepathy, for it to be possible with technology available to be used by mundane humans - telepathy is a Mind 3 Effect, and thus definitely beyond what is possible for mundane humans to do.<br /> <br /> In regards to prediction of outcomes - the Time and Entropy magickal Effects that allow predictions are superior to such an extent to prediction methods used by mundane humans, that I don't think they can be compared at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-29-2018, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T10:35:15-07:00","id":1231148,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Sphere levels necessary for an effect are particularly indicative of their innate cosmic difficulty.<br /> <br /> It takes three Masteries to make a new human, but Sleepers have managed it without coaching for quite a while.<br /> <br /> (If we use the historical era guidelines from the Book of Mirrors as a rubric, a new mythic age may have across-the-board drops in magical difficulties - so as the realm of the possible expands, the number of successes and scope of effects that mages can manage also makes some advances. There's likely no comparison between Sleepertech &quot;telepathy&quot; and a five or six success Mind effect, and having the former in the Consensus may make the latter easier to pull off.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":1653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","user":"Five Eyes","date":". 06-29-2018, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T23:28:29-07:00","id":1231307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1231148#post1231148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It takes three Masteries to make a new human, but Sleepers have managed it without coaching for quite a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>As authors of MtAs are not very good at either technology or actual occult you should expect such oversights. I personally think that you need 3 Masteries to create a fully functional, pre-programmed human being with a soul on spot. Otherwise you just need 2 humans and 9 month time, plus ~17+ years for a finished product, no magic or technology required. Sleepers can currently influence genetic makeup of the product (shoddily), but artificial womb is still far away. <br /> If you want to produce 'Victors' - life 3, reproduction oriented sanctum and some patience is all you really need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T15:07:18-07:00","id":1231460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1231104#post1231104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But for all we know technology will reach a point where telepathy and prediction of outcomes (and manipulating them) fall within the range of technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguably, telepathy is already possible, and has been for thousands of years. That is, if you define telepathy as &quot;transferring ideas from your head to someone else's&quot;. Under that definition, we most certainly have that already, using a process that is at once simple to describe, yet complex as any science.<br /> <br /> It's call &quot;Language&quot;.<br /> <br /> With but the use of arcane mouth sounds (with gestures and facial expressions thrown in for flavor), a person can transplant ideas into the minds of others. Of course, if you make the wrong mouth sounds at the wrong times, you'll end up scrambling the message you would send, or else implant a totally different idea than what you intended. Alternatively, those mouth sounds can make someone believe things that aren't true - even convince them to act directly against their own self-interest. And despite the old adage, these &quot;words&quot; can hurt people, even drive them to suicide.<br /> <br /> One step further, and you have writing. &quot;Words that stay&quot;. They affix ideas into a state that can be absorbed by a person thousands of miles away and hundreds of years in the future; your little markings in clay or stains on a page can convince people of your world view long after you're dead.<br /> <br /> <br /> This little thought experiment illustrates a point I've been making for a while now: every mundane act that modern people take for granted was a form of True Magick, once upon a time. Creating fire, cutting with a flint knife, and speaking words were all ancient, primordial bits of Awakened power at first. Before humans around these primeval Mages were convinced of the efficacy of these methods, and adopted them. First as Paths of sorcery, then as powers classified as Abilities. Some, like Language, are assumed to be possessed by a character by default, and only require a single experience or freebie point to buy more of. The form of telepathy involving words is so ingrained into the Consensus, you can just DO IT.<br /> <br /> It extends to more modern things. What is Drive but a form of Path of Conveyance that hit the mainstream? What is Firearms, but the same thing, but with specialized Devices pioneered in the Sorcerer's Crusade? What is Computer but a technomagic way of interacting with an entire virtual landscape (like the Digital Web, which even sleepers can visit with VR tech and sufficient knowledge)?<br /> <br /> With tech, the chain goes True Magick &gt; Wonder &gt; Sorcery Path &gt; Ability. The more the process is accepted, the more people adopt the Instruments of that process, until they aren't Instruments for magic anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T04:08:19-07:00","id":1231550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1231460#post1231460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arguably, telepathy is already possible, and has been for thousands of years. That is, if you define telepathy as &quot;transferring ideas from your head to someone else's&quot;. Under that definition, we most certainly have that already, using a process that is at once simple to describe, yet complex as any science.<br /> <br /> It's call &quot;Language&quot;.<br /> <br /> With but the use of arcane mouth sounds (with gestures and facial expressions thrown in for flavor), a person can transplant ideas into the minds of others. Of course, if you make the wrong mouth sounds at the wrong times, you'll end up scrambling the message you would send, or else implant a totally different idea than what you intended. Alternatively, those mouth sounds can make someone believe things that aren't true - even convince them to act directly against their own self-interest. And despite the old adage, these &quot;words&quot; can hurt people, even drive them to suicide.<br /> <br /> One step further, and you have writing. &quot;Words that stay&quot;. They affix ideas into a state that can be absorbed by a person thousands of miles away and hundreds of years in the future; your little markings in clay or stains on a page can convince people of your world view long after you're dead.<br /> <br /> <br /> This little thought experiment illustrates a point I've been making for a while now: every mundane act that modern people take for granted was a form of True Magick, once upon a time. Creating fire, cutting with a flint knife, and speaking words were all ancient, primordial bits of Awakened power at first. Before humans around these primeval Mages were convinced of the efficacy of these methods, and adopted them. First as Paths of sorcery, then as powers classified as Abilities. Some, like Language, are assumed to be possessed by a character by default, and only require a single experience or freebie point to buy more of. The form of telepathy involving words is so ingrained into the Consensus, you can just DO IT.<br /> <br /> It extends to more modern things. What is Drive but a form of Path of Conveyance that hit the mainstream? What is Firearms, but the same thing, but with specialized Devices pioneered in the Sorcerer's Crusade? What is Computer but a technomagic way of interacting with an entire virtual landscape (like the Digital Web, which even sleepers can visit with VR tech and sufficient knowledge)?<br /> <br /> With tech, the chain goes True Magick &gt; Wonder &gt; Sorcery Path &gt; Ability. The more the process is accepted, the more people adopt the Instruments of that process, until they aren't Instruments for magic anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking along somewhat similar lines while going through this thread. While the Technocrats speak a big game about making devices that improve the lives of everyday people, I wonder if people don't also benefit in such ways from the Traditions. As in, if the masses ended up accepting the capabilities of magic according to like, the Hermetic paradigm (or any other really), we could have possibly ended up in a similar place. On the other hand, this also makes me think that the Traditions probably also have many of the same problems that the Technocracy has (namely tyranny over not just society, but reality itself).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12226-houlio","name":"Houlio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T15:08:05-07:00","id":1231668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houlio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1231550#post1231550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking along somewhat similar lines while going through this thread. While the Technocrats speak a big game about making devices that improve the lives of everyday people, I wonder if people don't also benefit in such ways from the Traditions. As in, if the masses ended up accepting the capabilities of magic according to like, the Hermetic paradigm (or any other really), we could have possibly ended up in a similar place. On the other hand, this also makes me think that the Traditions probably also have many of the same problems that the Technocracy has (namely tyranny over not just society, but reality itself).</div> </div> </div> </div>I vaguely recall Brucato talking about the Mage's Fascist Urge in the M20 Book of Secrets. And how the very idea of having an exceptional person who can force their vision on reality inherently lends itself to autocratic thinking. Even if a mage doesn't want to be, their Awakened state makes it very easy to assume they know better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T17:20:35-07:00","id":1231688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1229454#post1229454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it is possible to create what is called a quantum computer.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean? We're already making prototypes. The tech may Seem fantastical, but then, so did phones, cars, and planes at one point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T06:27:41-07:00","id":1231786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1227452-real-technology-vs-the-technocracy-traditions?p=1231668#post1231668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I vaguely recall Brucato talking about the Mage's Fascist Urge in the M20 Book of Secrets. And how the very idea of having an exceptional person who can force their vision on reality inherently lends itself to autocratic thinking. Even if a mage doesn't want to be, their Awakened state makes it very easy to assume they know better.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only mass ascension which isn't inherently authoritarian is the kind where you simply create a world where people are able to seek their own personal gnosis more easily.<br /> <br /> For example, a messianic figure might want to create a world of peace and prosperity, where people of different creeds and faiths and nationalities live in harmony. And in such a scenario, people could find their own personal truth unhindered by fear or oppression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}